    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "64b39767"
      },
      "source": [
        "## ⚙️ Step 3: Feature Engineering & Train-Test Splitting\n",
        "\n",
        "To ensure our model generalizations are scientifically sound, we perform train-test splits before running any scaling algorithms. This fully prevents **data leakage**."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "a562bfa9"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Step 3-1: Split into Features (X) and Target (y)\n",
        "We will use the 10 mean characteristics (`features_mean`) as our feature set `X`, and the `diagnosis` column as our target variable `y`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "175b3fef",
        "outputId": "255bc842-93f9-433a-cf17-4cba2f737545"
      },
      "source": [
        "X = df[features_mean]\n",
        "y = df['diagnosis']\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Features (X) shape:\", X.shape)\n",
        "print(\"Target (y) shape:\", y.shape)"
      ],
      "execution_count": 72,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Features (X) shape: (569, 10)\n",
            "Target (y) shape: (569,)\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "7e1aedac"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Step 3-2: Train-Test Split\n",
        "We split the data first (e.g., 70% train, 30% test) to prevent any data leakage during scaling."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "3d9568f1",
        "outputId": "27f8ee53-2350-4ff9-c8b8-90a17fe9b9f8"
      },
      "source": [
        "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(X, y, test_size=0.3, random_state=42, stratify=y)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Training set size: {X_train.shape[0]} samples\")\n",
        "print(f\"Test set size: {X_test.shape[0]} samples\")"
      ],
      "execution_count": 73,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Training set size: 398 samples\n",
            "Test set size: 171 samples\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "8f164c9c"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Step 3-3: Standardize the Features\n",
        "We fit the `StandardScaler` only on the training set (`X_train`) and use it to transform both the training and testing sets."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "aeae7dd4",
        "outputId": "9c6003ab-3a79-4afe-a443-dbd1fa2f7715"
      },
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
        "\n",
        "scaler = StandardScaler()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Fit on training data and transform it\n",
        "X_train_scaled = scaler.fit_transform(X_train)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Only transform the test data\n",
        "X_test_scaled = scaler.transform(X_test)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Scaled sample from training set:\\n\", X_train_scaled[0])"
      ],
      "execution_count": 74,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Scaled sample from training set:\n",
            " [1.70581999 1.04974466 2.12129465 1.66933676 2.27645789 4.54429486\n",
            " 3.53913939 2.84839268 4.03238962 2.63977264]\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "193b8835"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Feature Scaling & Normalization\n",
        "\n",
        "Many distance-based and gradient-descent-based models (like KNN, SVM, Logistic Regression, and MLPs) require features to be on a uniform scale. We apply `StandardScaler` fitted exclusively on our training partitions."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "d6a71fc8"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Alternative: Using All 30 Features\n",
        "Here we split the dataset using all available features (excluding only the target column `diagnosis`) as suggested, scale them, and split them into training and testing sets."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "607fcb2f",
        "outputId": "9b41163c-5767-451d-8512-15757d134927"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Extract all features and the target\n",
        "X_all = df.drop('diagnosis', axis=1)\n",
        "y = df['diagnosis']\n",
        "\n",
        "# Train-Test Split\n",
        "X_train_all, X_test_all, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n",
        "    X_all, y, test_size=0.3, random_state=42, stratify=y\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Standardize all features\n",
        "scaler_all = StandardScaler()\n",
        "X_train_all_scaled = scaler_all.fit_transform(X_train_all)\n",
        "X_test_all_scaled = scaler_all.transform(X_test_all)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Using ALL features:\")\n",
        "print(\"X_train_all_scaled shape:\", X_train_all_scaled.shape)\n",
        "print(\"X_test_all_scaled shape:\", X_test_all_scaled.shape)"
      ],
      "execution_count": 75,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Using ALL features:\n",
            "X_train_all_scaled shape: (398, 30)\n",
            "X_test_all_scaled shape: (171, 30)\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "44a4e60e"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Compare Supervised Learning Algorithms\n",
        "We will define, train, and evaluate the 7 algorithms on both our 10-feature scaled dataset and our 30-feature scaled dataset."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 269
        },
        "id": "8c61d1fa",
        "outputId": "25196726-98e2-47a9-dbf1-7be29ef7c204"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Define the uniform random state\n",
        "RANDOM_STATE = 42\n",
        "\n",
        "# Initialize all 7 models using your custom hyperparameters\n",
        "models = {\n",
        "    'Naive Bayes': GaussianNB(),\n",
        "    'KNN': KNeighborsClassifier(n_neighbors=5),\n",
        "    'Decision Tree': DecisionTreeClassifier(max_depth=5, random_state=RANDOM_STATE),\n",
        "    'Random Forest': RandomForestClassifier(n_estimators=100, random_state=RANDOM_STATE),\n",
        "    'SVM': SVC(kernel='rbf', probability=True, random_state=RANDOM_STATE),\n",
        "    'Logistic Regression': LogisticRegression(max_iter=2000, random_state=RANDOM_STATE),\n",
        "    'ANN': MLPClassifier(hidden_layer_sizes=(64, 32), max_iter=1500, early_stopping=True, random_state=RANDOM_STATE)\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "results = []\n",
        "\n",
        "# Evaluate each model on both datasets\n",
        "for name, model in models.items():\n",
        "    # 1. 10 Features (Mean Only)\n",
        "    model.fit(X_train_scaled, y_train)\n",
        "    preds_10 = model.predict(X_test_scaled)\n",
        "    acc_10 = accuracy_score(y_test, preds_10)\n",
        "    rec_10 = recall_score(y_test, preds_10)\n",
        "    f1_10 = f1_score(y_test, preds_10)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # 2. 30 Features (All)\n",
        "    model.fit(X_train_all_scaled, y_train)\n",
        "    preds_30 = model.predict(X_test_all_scaled)\n",
        "    acc_30 = accuracy_score(y_test, preds_30)\n",
        "    rec_30 = recall_score(y_test, preds_30)\n",
        "    f1_30 = f1_score(y_test, preds_30)\n",
        "\n",
        "    results.append({\n",
        "        'Model': name,\n",
        "        '10-Feat Accuracy': acc_10,\n",
        "        '10-Feat Recall': rec_10,\n",
        "        '10-Feat F1': f1_10,\n",
        "        '30-Feat Accuracy': acc_30,\n",
        "        '30-Feat Recall': rec_30,\n",
        "        '30-Feat F1': f1_30\n",
        "    })\n",
        "\n",
        "# Convert results to DataFrame for nice visualization\n",
        "df_results = pd.DataFrame(results)\n",
        "display(df_results.sort_values(by='30-Feat Accuracy', ascending=False).style.format({\n",
        "    '10-Feat Accuracy': '{:.2%}', '10-Feat Recall': '{:.2%}', '10-Feat F1': '{:.2%}',\n",
        "    '30-Feat Accuracy': '{:.2%}', '30-Feat Recall': '{:.2%}', '30-Feat F1': '{:.2%}'\n",
        "}))"
      ],
