      "source": [
        "### Overfitting Analysis:\n",
        "The difference between training and testing accuracy provides an initial indication of how well a model generalizes to unseen data.\n",
        "1. **Good Generalization:** When training and testing accuracy are close, the model shows no strong indication of overfitting.\n",
        "2. **Potential Overfitting:** When training accuracy is considerably higher than testing accuracy, the model may have learned patterns specific to the training data.\n"
        "3. **Further Evaluation:** A small difference between training and testing accuracy does not prove that a model is completely free of overfitting. Cross-validation results should also be considered.\n"
        "In this experiment, Logistic Regression and KNN are evaluated using the 30-feature configuration. Their training and testing accuracy values, together with the 5-fold cross-validation results, provide a more reliable overview of their generalization performance."
      ]
    }
